IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fpa-dates`
IMPORT `fpa-rules`
IMPORT `fpa-beneficiary`
IMPORT `fpa-claimant`

-- Family Provision Act 1969 (ACT) -- worked cases for the questions of the beneficiary answering a claim, with mirror
-- cases: the s 20 question asked on the same facts from the claimant's seat and the beneficiary's, with answers that
-- agree.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the text before the file was run; none was copied from the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- (c) Australian Capital Territory. Used under CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). Unofficial text.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Short names used below`

yes MEANS TRUE
no MEANS FALSE

`10 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 10 3 2026
`1 May 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 5 2026
`10 Sep 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 10 9 2026
`11 Sep 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 11 9 2026

`THE PERSON PROVIDED FOR` MEANS `the person in whose favour the order was made (s 9A (4))`
`EACH ADMINISTRATOR` MEANS `each administrator of the estate (s 10 (1))`

§ `s 9A (2) -- applying to cut an order`

-- A beneficiary, an order standing: may apply.
#ASSERT `s 9A (2) -- can I apply to cut a provision order` yes yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No order standing (none made, or discharged): JUST FALSE (s 9A (1) "means").
#ASSERT `s 9A (2) -- can I apply to cut a provision order` yes no EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 9A (2) -- can I apply to cut a provision order` no no EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not a beneficiary: NOTHING (the grant limited in its own wording).
#ASSERT `s 9A (2) -- can I apply to cut a provision order` no yes EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `ss 9A, 10 -- whom must I serve` yes EQUALS LIST `THE PERSON PROVIDED FOR`, `EACH ADMINISTRATOR`
#ASSERT `ss 9A, 10 -- whom must I serve` no EQUALS EMPTY

§ `s 11 -- who bears the provision`

-- Argument order: the provision, my interest, all the bearing interests, an order for me, the court ordered otherwise,
-- a settled successive interest.
-- $60 000 provision; my interest $200 000 of $600 000: one third, $20 000.
#ASSERT `s 11 -- my share of the burden` 60000 200000 600000 no no no EQUALS JUST 20000
-- I am the only bearing beneficiary: the whole $60 000.
#ASSERT `s 11 -- my share of the burden` 60000 300000 300000 no no no EQUALS JUST 60000
-- $100 000 provision; my interest 1 of 3 parts: a third, unrounded.
#ASSERT `s 11 -- my share of the burden` 100000 1 3 no no no EQUALS JUST (100000 DIVIDED BY 3)
-- The court has ordered otherwise: NOTHING (its order decides).
#ASSERT `s 11 -- my share of the burden` 60000 200000 600000 no yes no EQUALS NOTHING
-- An order was made in my favour: I bear none (fork F9).
#ASSERT `s 11 -- my share of the burden` 60000 200000 600000 yes no no EQUALS JUST 0
-- A life interest under a settlement in the will: charged on the corpus, not apportioned to me (s 11 (3)).
#ASSERT `s 11 -- my share of the burden` 60000 200000 600000 no no yes EQUALS NOTHING
-- The bearing interests are worth nothing: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 11 -- my share of the burden` 60000 0 0 no no no EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 15 -- paying instead`

#ASSERT `s 15 -- can I be ordered to pay instead` yes yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 15 -- can I be ordered to pay instead` yes no EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15 -- can I be ordered to pay instead` no yes EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 20 -- property distributed to me, with mirror cases`

-- Argument order: made for a dependant, the grant, distributed on, notice first, vested.
-- Grant 10 March 2026; the 6 months end 10 September 2026.
#ASSERT `s 20 -- can property distributed to me be taken for the provision` yes `10 Mar 2026` `1 May 2026` yes no EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20 -- can property distributed to me be taken for the provision` no `10 Mar 2026` `11 Sep 2026` no yes EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20 -- can property distributed to me be taken for the provision` no `10 Mar 2026` `10 Sep 2026` no yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20 -- can property distributed to me be taken for the provision` no `10 Mar 2026` `11 Sep 2026` yes yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20 -- can property distributed to me be taken for the provision` no `10 Mar 2026` `11 Sep 2026` no no EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Mirror: the claimant's seat and the beneficiary's seat agree on the same facts.
#ASSERT `s 20 -- can property distributed to me be taken for the provision` no `10 Mar 2026` `11 Sep 2026` no yes EQUALS `s 20 -- can distributed property be used for my provision` no `10 Mar 2026` `11 Sep 2026` no yes
#ASSERT `s 20 -- can property distributed to me be taken for the provision` no `10 Mar 2026` `10 Sep 2026` no yes EQUALS `s 20 -- can distributed property be used for my provision` no `10 Mar 2026` `10 Sep 2026` no yes
#ASSERT `s 20 -- can property distributed to me be taken for the provision` yes `10 Mar 2026` `1 May 2026` yes no EQUALS `s 20 -- can distributed property be used for my provision` yes `10 Mar 2026` `1 May 2026` yes no
